          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"}> Bar-Natan 95, Def. 3.11 &amp; Theorem 7
            )
          %p
            In fact, when evaluated in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{\mathbf{N}}
            and under the identification (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "equivariant+K-theory#RelationToRepresentationTheory"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            of the point, these Adams operations on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagrams"} Jacobi diagrams
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operations"} Adams operations
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi q
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi q
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w_{\mathbf{N}}(\psi^q D)
                  \\;=\;
                  w_{\psi^q \mathbf{N}}(D)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"} Bar-Natan 95, Exc. 6.24
            )
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operation+on+Jacobi+diagrams"} Adams operation on Jacobi diagrams
          %h3#AsExpectationValuesOfSingleTraceOperators As expectation values of single trace observables
          %p
            We discuss how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
            on round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams"} chord diagrams
            arise in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+mechanics"} statistical mechanics
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+values"} expectation values
            of suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+trace+observables"} single trace observables
            subject to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick%27s+theorem"} Wick's theorem
          %p So consider
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                be a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi ρ
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}\otimes C \overset{\rho}{\to} C) \in \mathfrak{g}Mod
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representation"} Lie algebra representation
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p For comparison with traditional literature, choose
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi v
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v^a\}
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t^i\}
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            In terms of these linear bases, the representation is given by a sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho^i
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+matrices"} square matrices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big((\rho^i)^a{}_b\big)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\rho^i)^a{}_b v^b
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\rho(t^i, v^a)
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+summation+convention"} Einstein summation convention
            understood here and in the following.
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = (k_{i j})
            for the components of the Lie algebra metric in this basis, and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho_i \;\coloneqq\; k_{i j} \rho^j
          %p
            With all this understood, a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variable"} random variable
            with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z \;=\; Z_i \cdot \rho^i \;\;
          %p
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
            components
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z_i
          %p
            Now assume that the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z_i
            are
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+fields"} free fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variables"} random variables
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+distribution"} Gaussian distribution
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle Z_i \rangle \;=\; 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle Z_i Z_j \rangle \;=\; k_{i j}
          %p
            and such that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick%27s+theorem"} Wick's theorem
            applies to higher
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moments"} moments
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 4
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 4
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle Z_{i_1} Z_{i_2} Z_{i_3} Z_{i_4} \rangle
                  \\;=\;
                  k_{i_1 i_2} k_{i_3 i_4}
                  +
                  k_{i_1 i_3} k_{i_2 i_4}
                  +
                  k_{i_1 i_4} k_{i_2 i_3}
          %p etc.
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/expectation+values"} expectation values
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+trace+observables"} single trace observables
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ⟨
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi Z
                        %mi Z
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi Z
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-50%width", :width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi factors
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mi Z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi tr
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Big\langle
                  tr
                  \\big(
                  \\underset{
                  \\mathclap{
                  n\, factors
                  }
                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  Z Z \cdots Z
                  }
                  }
                  \\big)
                  \\Big\rangle
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\big\langle
                  Z_{i_1}
                  Z_{i_2}
                  \\cdots
                  Z_{i_n}
                  \\big\rangle
                  \\cdot
                  tr
                  \\big(
                  \\rho^{i_1}
                  \\cdot
                  \\rho^{i_2}
                  \\cdots
                  \\rho^{i_n}
                  \\big)
          %p
            Using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick%27s+theorem"} Wick's theorem
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ⟨
                          %mi tr
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi Z
                          %mi Z
                          %mi Z
                          %mi Z
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
