          %p etc.
          %p#TracedWickTheorem
            Here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick%27s+theorem"} Wick's theorem
            in the first lines is given by a sum over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+chord+diagrams"} linear chord diagrams
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            then serves to close these to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+chord+diagrams"} round chord diagrams
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SingleTraceOprtrAsWeightSystemOnChordDiagram.jpg", :width => "830"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            The values of the traces in the last line are the values of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_C
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
            which reflects the Wick-contractions modulo cyclic permutation.
          %p
            Essentially this observation (specifically for
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SYK-model"} SYK-model
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GGJJV18"} GGJJV 18, Section 2.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JiaVerbaarschot18"} Jia-Verbaarschot 18, Section 4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BNS18"} BNS 18, Section 2.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BINT18"} BINT 18, Section 2
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Narovlansky19"} Narovlansky 19, Slides 5-21
          %div
            %h3#AsLieWeightSystemsInBMNModel Chord diagrams as multi-trace observables in the BMN matrix model
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
              are temporally constant complex matrices which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+representations"} metric Lie representations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \otimes V \overset{\rho}{\to} V
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}=
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/su%282%29"} su(2)
              (interpreted as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-sphere"} fuzzy 2-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometries"} noncommutative geometries
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/giant+gravitons"} giant gravitons
              or equivalently as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+funnels"} fuzzy funnels
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D2+brane+bound+states"} D0-D2 brane bound states
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-sphere"} fuzzy 2-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rotation"} rotation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-trace+observable"} multi-trace observable
              on these supersymmetric states is hence an expression of the following form:
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/InvariantMultiTraceObservableOnBMNModelStates.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            %p
              Here we are showing the corresponding
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+notation"} Penrose notation
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+representations"} metric Lie representations
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  these multi-trace observables are encoded by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+chord+diagrams"} Sullivan chord diagrams
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %li
                %p
                  their value on the supersymmetric states
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔰𝔲
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi ρ
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{su}(2) \otimes V \overset{\rho}{\to}V
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
                  of the corresponding
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+system"} Lie algebra weight system
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi w
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{{}_V}
                  on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
              Or equivalently, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat D
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
              whose
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permuted
              closure is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "horizontal+chord+diagram#ClosureToSullivanChordDiagrams"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{V,\sigma}
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi D
                        %mo ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat D
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MultiTraceObservableFromSullivanChordDiagramII.jpg", :width => "800"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            %p
              But since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/all+horizontal+weight+systems+are+partitioned+Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} all horizontal weight systems are partitioned Lie algebra weight systems
              this way, this identifies supersymmetric states of the BMN matrix model as seen by invariant multi-trace observables as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagrams"} horizontal chord diagrams
              evaluated in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+weight+systems"} Lie algebra weight systems
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+double+line+notation"} 't Hooft double line notation
          %div
