            %p
              %br/
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots"} knots
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braids"} braids
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"}> chord diagram
                    ,
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+diagram"} Jacobi diagram
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+chord+diagram"} horizontal chord diagram
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1T+relation"}> 1T
                    \&amp;
                    %a{:href => "4T+relation#ForCircularChordDiagrams"} 4T relation
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2T+relation"}> 2T
                    \&amp;
                    %a{:href => "4T+relation#ForHorizontalChordDiagrams"}> 4T relation
                    \/
                    %br/
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+braid+relations"} infinitesimal braid relations
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+system"} weight system
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+system"} horizontal weight system
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+knot+invariant"} Vassiliev knot invariant
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+braid+invariant"} Vassiliev braid invariant
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems+are+associated+graded+of+Vassiliev+invariants"} weight systems are associated graded of Vassiliev invariants
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+systems+are+cohomology+of+loop+space+of+configuration+space"} horizontal weight systems are cohomology of loop space of configuration space
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Lie algebra weight systems motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Predrag+Cvitanovi%C4%87"}> Predrag Cvitanović
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Group theory for Feynman diagrams in non-Abelian gauge theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.14.1536"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.14.1536
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/108133"} spire:108133
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CvitanovicWeights76.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The concept of round Lie algebra weight systems for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
            originates around
          %ul
            %li#Kontsevich94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman diagrams and low-dimensional topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 120
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ihes.fr/~maxim/TEXTS/Feynman%20%20diagrams%20and%20low-dimensional%20topology.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BarNatan95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                , Section 2.4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Vassiliev knot invariants
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(95)93237-2"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(95)93237-2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.toronto.edu/drorbn/papers/OnVassiliev/OnVassiliev.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+systems"} horizontal weight systems
            in
          %ul
            %li#BarNatan96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vassiliev and Quantum Invariants of Braids
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9607001"} arxiv:q-alg/9607001
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#BarNatanStoimenow97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Stoimenow"} Alexander Stoimenow
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Fundamental Theorem of Vassiliev Invariants
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometry and Physics
              %strong 184
              Marcel Dekker Inc. (1996) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702009"}> arXiv:q-alg/9702009
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://users-math.au.dk/swann/Aarhus-proceedings-1995/index.html"} ISBN:0-8247-9791-4
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+representation"} fundamental
            = succeed "-weight" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤𝔩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{gl}(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+distance+kernels"} Cayley distance kernels
            on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
          %ul
            %li#CSS21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David Corfield
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Fundamental+weight+systems+are+quantum+states"} Fundamental weight systems are quantum states
              %strong 113
              112 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.02871"}> arXiv:2105.02871
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-023-01725-4"} doi:10.1007/s11005-023-01725-4
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Dmitry Khudoteplov, Elena Lanina, Alexey Sleptsov:
              %em Construction of Lie algebra weight system kernel via Vogel algebra
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.14417"}> arXiv:2411.14417
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#via_string_diagrams Via string diagrams
          %p
            From the construction given in
            %a{:href => "#BarNatan95"} Bar-Natan 95, Section 2.4
            the interpretation of
